-- title:
--   Coefficients in the maximal ideal force the value there
-- statement:
--   Let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}} =$ `AlgebraicClosure ℚ`, let $M$ be a nonzero natural number and $\ell$ a prime such that $A$-valuation of $\ell$ is $<1$ (so $\ell$ lies in the maximal ideal of $A$) and $\ell \nmid M$. Write $F_M$ for `laurentBaseChange (AlgebraicClosure ℚ) (modularFunctionFieldFull M)`, the subfield of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}((q))$ generated over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ by the coefficientwise images of the field $\mathbb{Q}(\,q\text{-expansions } j(q^d),\ d \mid M\,)$, where $j(q) = q^{-1}\cdot(\text{the rational power series } \mathrm{jNumQ})$. Let $w$ be a place of $F_M$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, i.e. a proper valuation subring of $F_M$ containing $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ and which is a principal ideal ring, and let $\mathrm{ord}_w$ be the associated order function, minus the logarithm of the $\mathbb{Z}^{m0}$-valued adic valuation attached to $w$. Assume: for some $a_0 \in A$ one has $\mathrm{ord}_w(\bar{j} - a_0) > 0$, where $\bar{j} \in F_M$ is the coefficientwise image of $j(q)$; the element $b \in F_M$ is a root of a monic polynomial over the subring of $F_M$ generated by the image of $A$ together with $\bar{j}$; and every Laurent coefficient $b_n$ ($n \in \mathbb{Z}$) of $b$ has $A$-valuation $<1$. Then for every $a \in A$ such that $b - a$ is a nonunit of the valuation subring of $w$, the $A$-valuation of $a$ is $<1$.
--
--   This is the $q$-expansion principle modulo the maximal ideal, in value form, for the modular function field of level $M$ prime to the residue characteristic $\ell$: a function integral over the chart ring $A[\bar{j}]$ whose Fourier coefficients all lie in the maximal ideal of $A$ can only take values in the maximal ideal at places lying over an $A$-integral value of $j$. It feeds the computations of Frobenius and inertia at the places of the special fibre of the degree-six model of the modular curve.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_valuation_lt_one_of_ord_sub_pos_of_coeff_lt_one.lean

